Grandpa: Ah, there you are, my boy! Welcome back to the island. It’s been too long, hasn’t it?
Grandpa: Come here and let me look at you. You’ve grown so tall and strong!
Grandpa: The last time I saw you, you barely reached my waist. How was the boat ride? The sea never changes, but I’m glad it brought you home safely.
Grandpa: Your room is ready, and I’ve baked your favorite bread just for tonight. You can still smell the warm dough in the air, can’t you?
Grandpa: Now, rest well, because tomorrow your work as a Data Annotator begins. Be up before the roosters, and meet me at the bakery while the stars are still out.
Grandpa: Welcome home, my boy. I’m proud to have you here.